title: The Rock is Jesus Christ, Not Peter
description: What the earliest church writers said about the rock of Matthew 16:18, set beside the King James text of Peter's confession.
output: lessons/heresies/heresies-that-rock-was-christ.html

# Rebuilt on the deck template from the hand-made page, with the author's 13 quotations exactly as the old page had them.
# Several of the quotations are paraphrases; the author keeps them as written.

=== Peter's confession
--- The Rock is Jesus Christ, Not Peter [title]
overline: Matthew 16 · Church Fathers Testimony
heading: The Rock is Jesus Christ, Not Peter
sub: What the earliest church actually taught
scripture: Matthew 16:15-18

=== The witnesses
--- Origen of Alexandria
kicker: 1 · c. 184–253 A.D.
quote: If we also say, ‘You are the Christ, the Son of the living God,’ we become Peter, and it can be said to us: ‘Upon this rock I will build my Church.’ | Origen of Alexandria, c. 184–253 A.D.

--- St. John Chrysostom
kicker: 2 · c. 349–407 A.D.
quote: Upon this rock I will build my Church, that is, upon the faith of his confession. | St. John Chrysostom, c. 349–407 A.D.

--- St. Hilary of Poitiers
kicker: 3 · c. 310–367 A.D.
quote: This faith is the foundation of the Church, for the Church is built upon this rock. | St. Hilary of Poitiers, c. 310–367 A.D.

--- St. Ambrose of Milan
kicker: 4 · c. 339–397 A.D.
quote: The rock is the faith upon which the Church is built. | St. Ambrose of Milan, c. 339–397 A.D.

--- St. Augustine of Hippo
kicker: 5 · 354–430 A.D.
quote: Christ did not say: you are the rock, but you are Peter. The rock was Christ. Peter was called rock because he confessed the Rock. The rock is the confession of faith Peter made: ‘You are the Christ, the Son of the living God.’ | St. Augustine of Hippo, 354–430 A.D.

--- Theodoret of Cyrus
kicker: 6 · c. 393–458 A.D.
quote: Blessed are you, Simon Bar-Jonah because you confessed the Truth. I say to you that you are Peter, and upon this rock of the confession of faith I will build My Church. | Theodoret of Cyrus, c. 393–458 A.D.

--- Eusebius of Caesarea
kicker: 7 · c. 260–339 A.D.
quote: The Church is built upon this confession of faith. | Eusebius of Caesarea, c. 260–339 A.D.

--- Clement of Alexandria
kicker: 8 · c. 150–215 A.D.
quote: Christ is called the Rock… because He is the foundation of all teaching. | Clement of Alexandria, c. 150–215 A.D.

--- Cyprian of Carthage
kicker: 9 · c. 200–258 A.D.
quote: The rest of the apostles were what Peter was, equal in honor and power. | Cyprian of Carthage, c. 200–258 A.D.

--- Jerome
kicker: 10 · c. 347–420 A.D.
quote: Upon this rock of confession the Church shall be built. | Jerome, c. 347–420 A.D.

--- Basil of Caesarea
kicker: 11 · c. 329–379 A.D.
quote: Do not say that the Church was built upon Peter… it was built upon the faith. | Basil of Caesarea, c. 329–379 A.D.

--- Gregory of Nyssa
kicker: 12 · c. 335–395 A.D.
quote: His Christocentric theology excludes the idea that the foundation of the Church is a man. He refers to Christ as the Rock, not Peter. | Gregory of Nyssa, c. 335–395 A.D.

--- Tertullian
kicker: 13 · c. 155–240 A.D.
quote: The Rock is Christ, not Peter. | Tertullian, c. 155–240 A.D.

=== Close
--- Thirteen witnesses
note: 13 Witnesses · 1st–5th Century · Matthew 16
scripture: Matthew 16:18
